 1929: // /**
 1930: //    For a point (x1,y1) inside the element and a line segment (x1,y1)-(x2,y2), find the intersection point 
 1931: //    (xIntersect,yIntersect) and the side (intersectingSide) that it intersects.
 1932: 
 1933: //    Inputs:
 1934: //    @param x1, y1: point inside the element
 1935: //    @param x2, y2: other end of the line segment
 1936: 
 1937: //    Outputs:
 1938: //    @param intersectingSide:  side that intersects the line segment
 1939: //    @param nextElement: element that contains the intersection point
 1940: //    @param xIntersect, yIntersect: intersection point  
 1941: 
 1942: //    The equations for the two segments (the one we are considering and one of the sides of the element) are:
 1943: //    P1(tt1) = (x1,y1) + tt1*(x2-x1, y2-y1)  where 0 <= tt1 <= 1
 1944: //    P2(tt2) = (x3,y3) + tt2*(x4-x3, y4-y3)  where 0 <= tt2 <= 1
 1945: 
 1946: //    If the two segments are parallel, they do not intersect. This is checked by the determinant of the two vectors
 1947: //    (Delta) being zero.
 1948: 
 1949: //    The intersection point happens when:
 1950: //    tt1(x2-x1) - tt2(x4-x3) = x3-x1
 1951: //    tt1(y2-y1) - tt2(y4-y3) = y3-y1
 1952:    
 1953: //    Assumption: the 4 points (including those of the side segment) are different.
 1954: //    The eqs. for the 2 lines are: X=X1+(X2-X1)*tt1 and X=X3+(X4-X3)*tt2.	
 1955: //    Output: false: no intersection or colinear; true: exactly 1 intersection.	
 1956: //    If true, (xIntersect,yIntersect) is the intersection.				
 1957: //    Modified to only check tt2, assuming 0<=tt1<=1 is already assured. 
 1958: // **/
 1959: // __inline__ __device__ bool Element::findPathIntersection(double x1, double y1, double x2, double y2, 
 1960: //                                                          Side& intersectingSide, Element& nextElement,
